1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:02,244
June 18, 2019.

2
00:00:02,244 --> 00:00:06,419
The Eastern Pacific, off the coast of Colombia.

3
00:00:07,119 --> 00:00:10,053
A Coast Guard boat is running down something

4
00:00:10,053 --> 00:00:12,321
that barely rises above the waves.

5
00:00:12,321 --> 00:00:15,322
A long, low, gray hull, about fifty feet from

6
00:00:15,322 --> 00:00:16,056
end to end.

7
00:00:16,056 --> 00:00:18,857
ABC News reported it was making around ten

8
00:00:18,857 --> 00:00:19,791
miles an hour.

9
00:00:20,391 --> 00:00:23,265
Someone shouts at it to stop, in Spanish.

10
00:00:23,265 --> 00:00:24,807
The hull keeps moving.

11
00:00:25,607 --> 00:00:28,115
So the boarding team goes aboard anyway.

12
00:00:28,115 --> 00:00:29,745
While it's still underway.

13
00:00:30,645 --> 00:00:32,765
One of them pounds on the hatch.

14
00:00:32,765 --> 00:00:33,891
Again, and again.

15
00:00:33,891 --> 00:00:36,341
And then it opens, and hands come up.

16
00:00:37,341 --> 00:00:37,933
Inside:

17
00:00:37,933 --> 00:00:42,077
five people, and almost 17,000 pounds of cocaine.

18
00:00:43,177 --> 00:00:45,794
The Coast Guard released video of the boarding

19
00:00:45,794 --> 00:00:48,639
in July, and President Trump shared it on Twitter.

20
00:00:49,239 --> 00:00:51,816
So how do you find one low gray hull in a

21
00:00:51,816 --> 00:00:54,708
patch of ocean more than twice the size of the

22
00:00:54,708 --> 00:00:56,342
continental United States?

23
00:00:56,342 --> 00:00:58,731
Who builds a submarine out of wood and

24
00:00:58,731 --> 00:01:00,240
fiberglass, in a jungle?

25
00:01:00,240 --> 00:01:03,069
And what became of the five people inside, as

26
00:01:03,069 --> 00:01:04,577
far as the record shows?

27
00:01:05,777 --> 00:01:08,103
Case file 024.

28
00:01:10,503 --> 00:01:14,364
This is the story of a single patrol, in 2019.

29
00:01:14,864 --> 00:01:17,810
The ship behind that boat is the Coast Guard

30
00:01:17,810 --> 00:01:18,680
Cutter Munro.

31
00:01:18,680 --> 00:01:21,626
A national security cutter, the sixth of its

32
00:01:21,626 --> 00:01:24,170
class, commissioned in 2017, home port

33
00:01:24,170 --> 00:01:25,509
Alameda, California.

34
00:01:26,009 --> 00:01:29,032
It was on its first counter-drug patrol.

35
00:01:29,032 --> 00:01:31,449
98 days, in the Eastern Pacific.

36
00:01:32,249 --> 00:01:34,967
The Eastern Pacific is where most of the Coast

37
00:01:34,967 --> 00:01:36,976
Guard's drug interdictions happen.

38
00:01:36,976 --> 00:01:39,517
About three quarters of them, in a patch of

39
00:01:39,517 --> 00:01:41,999
ocean of roughly six million square miles.

40
00:01:42,899 --> 00:01:45,743
Here's the arithmetic the crews live with.

41
00:01:45,743 --> 00:01:48,587
ABC News reported that the Coast Guard can

42
00:01:48,587 --> 00:01:51,702
identify about 85% of the smuggling out there,

43
00:01:51,702 --> 00:01:54,816
but has the resources to go after only about a

44
00:01:54,816 --> 00:01:56,509
quarter of those vessels.

45
00:01:57,509 --> 00:01:59,989
Munro also carried a helicopter crew from

46
00:01:59,989 --> 00:02:02,167
HITRON, the Coast Guard's Helicopter

47
00:02:02,167 --> 00:02:04,042
Interdiction Tactical Squadron.

48
00:02:04,042 --> 00:02:06,522
The Coast Guard said the helicopter fired

49
00:02:06,522 --> 00:02:08,881
disabling shots into the engines of two

50
00:02:08,881 --> 00:02:11,422
fleeing boats, so the boarding teams could

51
00:02:11,422 --> 00:02:12,208
take control.

52
00:02:12,808 --> 00:02:15,382
By the end, Munro's crew had made eight

53
00:02:15,382 --> 00:02:16,307
interdictions.

54
00:02:17,207 --> 00:02:19,611
Seven of the eight were ordinary boats.

55
00:02:19,611 --> 00:02:22,817
The eighth was the one that looked like a submarine.

56
00:02:24,017 --> 00:02:26,853
Self-propelled semi-submersibles sound more

57
00:02:26,853 --> 00:02:28,369
official than they are.

58
00:02:28,869 --> 00:02:31,414
They're built in makeshift yards on jungle

59
00:02:31,414 --> 00:02:34,079
riverbanks in Colombia, mostly from wood and

60
00:02:34,079 --> 00:02:34,745
fiberglass.

61
00:02:34,745 --> 00:02:37,532
They ride so low that only the top of the hull

62
00:02:37,532 --> 00:02:39,894
and a small hatch show above the water.

63
00:02:39,894 --> 00:02:42,681
And the exhaust is altered to cut the engine's

64
00:02:42,681 --> 00:02:43,589
heat signature.

65
00:02:44,289 --> 00:02:47,685
USNI News reported in 2019 that these boats

66
00:02:47,685 --> 00:02:51,081
can carry up to 5,000 kilograms a shipment.

67
00:02:51,081 --> 00:02:53,134
That's over 11,000 pounds.

68
00:02:53,134 --> 00:02:56,688
Fishing boats and go-fasts usually top out at

69
00:02:56,688 --> 00:02:57,793
900 kilograms.

70
00:02:58,793 --> 00:03:01,638
A build costs somewhere between half a million

71
00:03:01,638 --> 00:03:04,359
dollars and a million, Defense Media Network

72
00:03:04,359 --> 00:03:05,410
reported in 2010.

73
00:03:05,410 --> 00:03:08,564
The cargo aboard can be worth hundreds of millions.

74
00:03:09,264 --> 00:03:11,962
And many of these boats have a scuttle valve.

75
00:03:11,962 --> 00:03:14,600
Open it, and the boat and the evidence go to

76
00:03:14,600 --> 00:03:17,179
the bottom, and the crew has to be rescued.

77
00:03:18,079 --> 00:03:20,773
One of the first, nicknamed Bigfoot, was

78
00:03:20,773 --> 00:03:23,804
sighted in November 2006, a hundred miles off

79
00:03:23,804 --> 00:03:26,903
Costa Rica, carrying three tons of cocaine and

80
00:03:26,903 --> 00:03:27,913
a crew of four.

81
00:03:28,613 --> 00:03:31,263
Defense Media Network reported that for two

82
00:03:31,263 --> 00:03:32,373
years this worked.

83
00:03:32,373 --> 00:03:34,900
Crews scuttled their boats, interdictions

84
00:03:34,900 --> 00:03:37,550
turned into rescues, and the smugglers were

85
00:03:37,550 --> 00:03:39,152
sent home without charges.

86
00:03:39,852 --> 00:03:42,263
Defense Media Network described the problem

87
00:03:42,263 --> 00:03:42,767
this way.

88
00:03:42,767 --> 00:03:45,122
Boarding one of these at night, with water

89
00:03:45,122 --> 00:03:47,420
splashing over the boarding team's boots.

90
00:03:47,420 --> 00:03:49,887
And, the Christian Science Monitor reported,

91
00:03:49,887 --> 00:03:52,353
the crew could sink the boat within moments.

92
00:03:53,053 --> 00:03:55,882
Then, in September 2008, the Coast Guard

93
00:03:55,882 --> 00:03:58,924
seized two semi-submersibles, each carrying

94
00:03:58,924 --> 00:04:00,904
about seven tons of cocaine.

95
00:04:01,504 --> 00:04:03,885
Within a month, Congress passed the Drug

96
00:04:03,885 --> 00:04:06,027
Trafficking Vessel Interdiction Act.

97
00:04:06,027 --> 00:04:08,646
It made it a crime to run one of these boats

98
00:04:08,646 --> 00:04:10,908
covertly through international waters.

99
00:04:10,908 --> 00:04:13,646
Prosecutors no longer needed a bale of cocaine

100
00:04:13,646 --> 00:04:14,539
to make a case.

101
00:04:15,539 --> 00:04:18,269
In July 2015, the cutter Stratton boarded one

102
00:04:18,269 --> 00:04:18,936
off Mexico.

103
00:04:18,936 --> 00:04:21,666
Vice reported 14,000 pounds of cocaine, and a

104
00:04:21,666 --> 00:04:24,093
boarding that took under thirty seconds.

105
00:04:24,093 --> 00:04:26,763
The officer shouted for a crowbar and heaved

106
00:04:26,763 --> 00:04:29,190
at the hatch, then yelled in Spanish for

107
00:04:29,190 --> 00:04:30,464
everyone to come out.

108
00:04:30,464 --> 00:04:33,012
Munro's boarding four years later would be

109
00:04:33,012 --> 00:04:35,378
called the Coast Guard's largest single

110
00:04:35,378 --> 00:04:36,531
seizure since 2015.

111
00:04:37,131 --> 00:04:40,608
Put side by side, the milestones look like this.

112
00:04:41,908 --> 00:04:43,807
Back to June eighteenth.

113
00:04:44,307 --> 00:04:47,244
ABC News reported the sub was first spotted

114
00:04:47,244 --> 00:04:48,132
from the air.

115
00:04:48,132 --> 00:04:51,411
Munro launched two smaller boats to run it down.

116
00:04:52,011 --> 00:04:55,153
The Drug Enforcement Administration later put

117
00:04:55,153 --> 00:04:57,877
the location at about 92 nautical miles

118
00:04:57,877 --> 00:04:59,972
northwest of Tumaco, Colombia.

119
00:04:59,972 --> 00:05:02,696
It described the vessel as a fifty-foot

120
00:05:02,696 --> 00:05:05,280
semi-submersible with a sealed cabin.

121
00:05:06,080 --> 00:05:09,300
Then comes the part the Coast Guard put on video.

122
00:05:09,300 --> 00:05:10,943
The boat pulls alongside.

123
00:05:10,943 --> 00:05:13,178
Someone yells at the crew to stop.

124
00:05:13,178 --> 00:05:14,229
The sub doesn't.

125
00:05:15,029 --> 00:05:17,529
A boarding team member gets onto the hull.

126
00:05:17,529 --> 00:05:19,910
Water is breaking over the deck, and the

127
00:05:19,910 --> 00:05:21,696
footage jolts with every wave.

128
00:05:21,696 --> 00:05:23,541
A crewman hammers on the hatch.

129
00:05:24,341 --> 00:05:25,777
It opens. Hands go up.

130
00:05:25,777 --> 00:05:28,582
The faces of the people who climbed out are

131
00:05:28,582 --> 00:05:29,952
blurred in the video.

132
00:05:31,052 --> 00:05:33,684
Five people were arrested.

133
00:05:33,684 --> 00:05:35,303
Inside the hull:

134
00:05:35,303 --> 00:05:38,036
7,683 kilograms of cocaine.

135
00:05:38,036 --> 00:05:40,161
Almost 17,000 pounds.

136
00:05:41,161 --> 00:05:44,610
The Coast Guard valued it at $232 million.

137
00:05:44,610 --> 00:05:46,827
The DEA's figure was lower:

138
00:05:46,827 --> 00:05:48,388
about $192 million.

139
00:05:48,388 --> 00:05:51,508
Same cocaine, two different estimates.

140
00:05:52,508 --> 00:05:55,474
Munro's commanding officer, Captain James

141
00:05:55,474 --> 00:05:58,658
Estramonte, told ABC News, quote, this is as

142
00:05:58,658 --> 00:06:00,250
satisfying as it gets.

143
00:06:00,250 --> 00:06:03,289
He called it the largest bust in the Coast

144
00:06:03,289 --> 00:06:04,519
Guard since 2015.

145
00:06:05,719 --> 00:06:08,513
Three weeks later, Munro came into port.

146
00:06:09,013 --> 00:06:12,065
On July eleventh, the crew offloaded at Naval

147
00:06:12,065 --> 00:06:14,710
Air Station North Island, in San Diego.

148
00:06:14,710 --> 00:06:17,761
Pallets of cocaine wrapped in plastic, lifted

149
00:06:17,761 --> 00:06:19,253
off the deck by crane.

150
00:06:19,953 --> 00:06:23,512
The total was more than 39,000 pounds of

151
00:06:23,512 --> 00:06:26,804
cocaine, and 933 pounds of marijuana.

152
00:06:26,804 --> 00:06:30,897
The Coast Guard put the value at $569 million.

153
00:06:31,897 --> 00:06:34,874
That figure included about eight thousand

154
00:06:34,874 --> 00:06:37,053
pounds from two other cutters.

155
00:06:37,053 --> 00:06:40,320
Munro's own eight interdictions accounted for

156
00:06:40,320 --> 00:06:43,951
more than 31,000 pounds, worth about $467 million.

157
00:06:44,751 --> 00:06:47,635
Vice President Mike Pence attended the offload.

158
00:06:47,635 --> 00:06:50,458
He told the crew that fourteen operations went

159
00:06:50,458 --> 00:06:53,097
into the offload, and that one of them, the

160
00:06:53,097 --> 00:06:55,859
semi-submersible, was the largest Coast Guard

161
00:06:55,859 --> 00:06:57,209
removal in four years.

162
00:06:57,909 --> 00:07:00,506
He added that the Coast Guard was, quote,

163
00:07:00,506 --> 00:07:03,229
seizing illegal drugs at a faster rate than

164
00:07:03,229 --> 00:07:03,989
ever before.

165
00:07:05,089 --> 00:07:07,777
Vice Admiral Linda Fagan, who commanded the

166
00:07:07,777 --> 00:07:10,402
Coast Guard's Pacific Area, said her crews

167
00:07:10,402 --> 00:07:12,965
were facing the highest levels of cocaine

168
00:07:12,965 --> 00:07:14,903
cultivation and smuggling ever.

169
00:07:15,703 --> 00:07:17,996
Not every chase ends in a seizure.

170
00:07:17,996 --> 00:07:20,963
USNI News reported that smugglers often dump

171
00:07:20,963 --> 00:07:24,065
their loads before the pursuit boats catch up.

172
00:07:24,765 --> 00:07:26,911
And critics say it isn't enough.

173
00:07:26,911 --> 00:07:29,594
Sanho Tree, a drug policy analyst at the

174
00:07:29,594 --> 00:07:32,545
Institute for Policy Studies, told ABC News,

175
00:07:32,545 --> 00:07:35,965
quote, we're only catching a fraction of the drugs.

176
00:07:37,065 --> 00:07:40,127
USNI News reported that officials estimated

177
00:07:40,127 --> 00:07:43,330
the Coast Guard, together with other agencies

178
00:07:43,330 --> 00:07:46,392
and partner nations, stops about 11% of the

179
00:07:46,392 --> 00:07:49,311
illegal drug flow into the United States.

180
00:07:50,611 --> 00:07:53,789
Five people on a sub means a prosecution.

181
00:07:54,289 --> 00:07:57,089
The case went to federal court in the Middle

182
00:07:57,089 --> 00:08:00,016
District of Florida, investigated by the DEA's

183
00:08:00,016 --> 00:08:02,879
Panama Express Strike Force in Tampa, working

184
00:08:02,879 --> 00:08:05,615
with the Coast Guard Investigative Service,

185
00:08:05,615 --> 00:08:08,479
the FBI, Homeland Security Investigations and

186
00:08:08,479 --> 00:08:08,924
others.

187
00:08:09,624 --> 00:08:12,219
Three men pleaded guilty, in August and

188
00:08:12,219 --> 00:08:13,416
September of 2019.

189
00:08:13,416 --> 00:08:16,344
On December eighteenth, they were sentenced.

190
00:08:17,244 --> 00:08:20,343
Carlos Chavez-Aguirre, thirty-five, got twenty

191
00:08:20,343 --> 00:08:20,747
years.

192
00:08:20,747 --> 00:08:23,577
Yesid Caicedo Asprilla, fifty, got twelve.

193
00:08:23,577 --> 00:08:26,878
David Hurtado Vallecilla, forty-five, got eleven.

194
00:08:26,878 --> 00:08:29,843
All three are Colombian nationals, convicted

195
00:08:29,843 --> 00:08:32,874
of conspiring to distribute five kilograms or

196
00:08:32,874 --> 00:08:35,906
more of cocaine aboard a vessel bound for the

197
00:08:35,906 --> 00:08:36,849
United States.

198
00:08:38,049 --> 00:08:40,754
The DEA said two other defendants were

199
00:08:40,754 --> 00:08:43,602
scheduled to be sentenced in January and

200
00:08:43,602 --> 00:08:44,812
February of 2020.

201
00:08:45,612 --> 00:08:48,576
The prosecutions around these boats kept going.

202
00:08:48,576 --> 00:08:51,161
In March 2020, a Colombian man, Alexander

203
00:08:51,161 --> 00:08:53,683
Giraldo Santa, pleaded guilty to cocaine

204
00:08:53,683 --> 00:08:56,205
conspiracy, and admitted he helped build

205
00:08:56,205 --> 00:08:57,340
semi-submersibles.

206
00:08:57,340 --> 00:09:00,114
The DEA said the Coast Guard intercepted two

207
00:09:00,114 --> 00:09:00,619
of them.

208
00:09:00,619 --> 00:09:03,267
The release doesn't say whether either was

209
00:09:03,267 --> 00:09:04,087
Munro's boat.

210
00:09:04,787 --> 00:09:07,657
And in May 2023, a federal judge in Tampa

211
00:09:07,657 --> 00:09:10,878
sentenced Oscar Adriano Quintero Rengifo, whom

212
00:09:10,878 --> 00:09:13,398
Colombian media called the Prince of

213
00:09:13,398 --> 00:09:16,549
Semi-Submersibles, to 20 years and 10 months.

214
00:09:16,549 --> 00:09:19,559
Prosecutors said the Coast Guard stopped at

215
00:09:19,559 --> 00:09:22,570
least four vessels tied to his organization

216
00:09:22,570 --> 00:09:25,721
between 2015 and 2019, two of them semi-subs,

217
00:09:25,721 --> 00:09:29,011
carrying more than 13,000 kilograms of cocaine.

218
00:09:29,011 --> 00:09:32,162
The release doesn't say whether the Munro sub

219
00:09:32,162 --> 00:09:33,282
was one of them.

220
00:09:34,382 --> 00:09:36,601
What does one patrol tell you?

221
00:09:37,101 --> 00:09:40,500
Munro's patrol was a snapshot of the contest at sea.

222
00:09:40,500 --> 00:09:43,508
A cutter, a helicopter, two small boats, and a

223
00:09:43,508 --> 00:09:46,188
team willing to step onto a hull that was

224
00:09:46,188 --> 00:09:47,234
built to vanish.

225
00:09:48,034 --> 00:09:50,795
At the offload, Admiral Fagan pointed at the

226
00:09:50,795 --> 00:09:51,862
other side of it.

227
00:09:51,862 --> 00:09:54,309
About 70% of the Coast Guard's offshore

228
00:09:54,309 --> 00:09:56,882
presence, she said, was an aging fleet of

229
00:09:56,882 --> 00:09:59,580
medium-endurance cutters, many of them more

230
00:09:59,580 --> 00:10:00,898
than fifty years old.

231
00:10:01,698 --> 00:10:04,090
Vice President Pence said the Coast Guard

232
00:10:04,090 --> 00:10:06,774
deserved better, and pledged to fully fund it,

233
00:10:06,774 --> 00:10:08,525
including replacing old ships.

234
00:10:09,425 --> 00:10:12,297
The boarding and the offload happened in 2019.

235
00:10:12,297 --> 00:10:14,045
The court updates run later.

236
00:10:14,045 --> 00:10:16,730
Footage that isn't from the June eighteenth

237
00:10:16,730 --> 00:10:18,790
boarding is labeled file footage.

238
00:10:19,690 --> 00:10:22,442
That day, a boat carrying almost 17,000 pounds

239
00:10:22,442 --> 00:10:25,135
of cocaine, worth well over a hundred million

240
00:10:25,135 --> 00:10:28,246
dollars, was stopped, and five people were arrested.

241
00:10:28,246 --> 00:10:30,999
Three were later sentenced to eleven to twenty

242
00:10:30,999 --> 00:10:31,358
years.

243
00:10:31,358 --> 00:10:33,990
The record I found doesn't say what happened

244
00:10:33,990 --> 00:10:35,007
to the other two.

245
00:10:36,307 --> 00:10:38,561
Sources are in the description.

246
00:10:38,561 --> 00:10:41,833
I'm Cold Warrant, and this was case file 024.
